<title>INDIA: India approves Larsen, Samsung venture.</title>
<headline>India approves Larsen, Samsung venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Industry Ministry said on Monday it approved a proposal of Larsen and Toubro Ltd to set up a 50-50 joint venture with South Korea's Samsung Electronics to make telecommunications equipment.</p>
<p>The joint venture, involving financial and technical collaboration between the two firms, will have a foreign direct investment of 375 million rupees ($10.5 million), a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>($1=35.70 rupees)</p>
</text>
